[thin] Numerical threshold classification at the nominal 3 mm keeper plate. Its two analytic native faces are Z0 and Z3 in the manufacturing frame; the reported anchors span the complete 3.000 mm section. The warning does not identify a sub-3 mm section. The plate fits the 3.5 mm wall slot with 0.25 mm room on each face.
alternatives: Use the exact native plane spacing to interpret the strict threshold. Increasing the keeper thickness solely to change floating-point ranking consumes its sliding allowance; reducing it creates a thinner bearing plate.
